.TH PIANO-SENSORS-CHECK 1 "October 2026" "piano" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
piano-sensors-check \- inspect piano rotation gates after a fresh boot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B piano-sensors-check
.RB [ --orientations ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run as the active GNOME Wayland user, without sudo. The script requests sudo
only for input classification, switch-state ioctls, libinput capabilities and
system logs. It does not grab input, change settings or restart services.
Install libinput-tools to include libinput capability reporting.
.PP
Print package versions, session identity, effective sensor udev properties,
SW_TABLET_MODE, Mutter PanelOrientationManaged, orientation lock, current
monitor configuration, and five seconds of monitor-sensor output.
.PP
With --orientations, prompt for docked landscape, detached top/left/bottom/right
edges up, and redocking. Record visual rotation and four-corner touch results.
Use a terminal on stdin; output can be piped to tee. Keep logs private.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the reporting commands completed. It is not a hardware acceptance
result. Nonzero indicates missing inspection tools, failed reporting or an
unsuitable session. Interrupting the script does not change device state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR monitor-sensor (1),
.BR libinput (1),
.BR busctl (1)
